capnp-compiler

The behaviour of this compiler — grammar, name resolution, type-id derivation and the struct layout
algorithm — follows the Cap'n Proto reference compiler (C++), which we read to understand and then
re-implemented in Rust:

  Cap'n Proto — Copyright (c) 2013-2017 Sandstorm Development Group, Inc.; Cloudflare, Inc.;
  and other contributors. Licensed under the MIT License. https://capnproto.org

Thank you to everyone who built Cap'n Proto and capnproto-rust.

The files under std/capnp/ (the Cap'n Proto standard schema files) are included unchanged from the
Cap'n Proto distribution so that imports such as "/capnp/c++.capnp" resolve exactly as with the
official compiler. They remain under the MIT License of the Cap'n Proto project (copyright as above);
std/capnp/rust.capnp comes from capnproto-rust (MIT, David Renshaw and contributors).

AI collaboration: design and code were written with the help of AI (Claude, Anthropic). Review is done by
humans and by further checks (tests against the official compiler, CI gates).

